Through the original data.txt we look at the first bytes to determine what compression command was used.
     bandit12@bandit:~$ cat data.txt 
     00000000: 1f8b 0808 a6f0 3b6a 0203 6461 7461 322e  ......;j..data2.

we can see it starts with 1f8b 08
This is the compression of gzip

So we move the file to a gzip format and decompress it.
    bandit12@bandit:/tmp/tmp.Ibue94e8OL$ mv hexdump compressed.gz
    bandit12@bandit:/tmp/tmp.Ibue94e8OL$ ls
    compressed.gz  data.txt
    bandit12@bandit:/tmp/tmp.Ibue94e8OL$ gzip -d compressed.gz 
    bandit12@bandit:/tmp/tmp.Ibue94e8OL$ ls
    compressed  data.txt
